From f0e1cb0052436b10aa096c1bba9b8a010fbbdbe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 08:25:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dashboard: WAN enable/disable switch and a USB disk selector

Two controls the stock Network Map carried, brought over to the dashboard that
replaced it (standing rule 39 retired index.asp; nothing had taken these over).

Internet card, upper right: a WAN enable/disable switch bound to the PRIMARY
unit. It posts wan_unit + wan_enable to /start_apply.htm with
action_script=restart_wan_if, which is the same path device-map/internet.asp
used - validate_apply() rewrites wan_enable to wanN_enable once it has seen
wan_unit (web.c:4379/4540), the action_script picks the unit back up
(web.c:6202), and start_wan_if() then returns at its wanN_enable check
(rc/wan.c:1351). The state is therefore persistent across a reboot rather than
a session-only disconnect. wan_unit is emitted BEFORE wan_enable because
validate_apply walks the posted vars in order.

The switch is neutral grey per standing rule 11; only OFF, the abnormal state,
borrows a colour. Turning the internet off asks for confirmation first, turning
it back on does not. It is hidden outside router/WISP modes, where wanN_enable
has no meaning, and the live poll now also reads wanN_enable so the control
stays honest if the WAN is changed from another tab, the CLI or a failover.

Storage card: a device selector appears once two or more USB disks are
attached, replacing the old "+N more disk attached" line - selecting a disk
repoints the ring, name and capacity at it. get_usb_info() reports storage only
(ej_get_usb_info hardcodes deviceType "storage"), so every entry is something
the ring can describe; a disk with nothing mounted reads "Not mounted" rather
than a misleading 0%. The option list is rebuilt only when the attached set
actually changes, because the boot poll re-renders every 5s and a blind rebuild
would shut an open dropdown under the user. The selection is keyed on node +
name so it survives that re-render.

Also fixes a pre-existing defect in the Internet poll that this feature would
have tripped: it scheduled the next tick only after a 200, so a single failed
request killed the chain for the rest of the session - and a WAN restart is
exactly what takes httpd's answers away. Rewritten with the standing rule 34
one-shot guard so every completion path reschedules exactly once, without
touching the UI on a failure.

i18n: RDSH_87-89 appended to all 25 packs (English pending translation);
everything else reuses existing keys. Tokens are in backticks or double-quoted
attributes per standing rule 29.

Verified without a build: reaper_langcheck 0 breakers; 100 inline script blocks
parse clean under node in all 25 languages; ASCII-only; mock-router render plus
CDP drive of both controls (dropdown repoints the ring across mounted and
unmounted disks, first click opens the dialog without submitting, cancel
applies nothing, confirm posts wan_unit=0 wan_enable=0 restart_wan_if).
Metal validation owed.
